efault_fair_val":373.49,"premium_pct":-39.6,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":18.4,"pe_forward":16.2,"pb_trailing":5,"pb_forward":4.5,"div_yield":0,"ps_ratio":2.8,"fcf_to_ev":5.14,"fcf_to_mcap":9.04,"liab_to_assets":102.3,"cash_to_assets":20.7,"current_ratio":0.88,"roe":18,"roa":10.8,"moat":{"ticker":"IT","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Gartner 作為 IT 研究與顧問領域的領導者，擁有強大的品牌聲譽和專業知識，使其能夠收取高額的諮詢與研究報告費用。客戶高度依賴 Gartner 的獨立分析來做出關鍵的技術決策，這形成了顯著的品牌護城河。相較於其他資訊提供者，Gartner 的報告和數據具有更高的權威性和參考價值，客戶難以找到完全替代的方案。這種品牌忠誠度和對專業知識的依賴，賦予了 Gartner 相當的定價權，使其能夠在市場中維持穩定的利潤率。","comment_en":"Gartner, as a leader in IT research and advisory, possesses a strong brand reputation and expertise, enabling it to charge premium prices for its consulting and research reports. Clients heavily rely on Gartner's independent analysis for critical technology decisions, forming a significant brand moat. Compared to other information providers, Gartner's reports and data hold higher authority and reference value, making it difficult for clients to find complete substitutes. This brand loyalty and reliance on expertise grant Gartner considerable pricing power, allowing it to maintain stable profit margins in the market."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Gartner 的核心競爭力在於其研究方法、數據庫和分析師的專業知識，而非受專利或特許權保護的技術。雖然其研究方法論可能具有一定的獨特性，但並非嚴格意義上的專利壁壘，容易被競爭對手模仿或開發類似的分析框架。行業監管對其影響也相對較小，沒有顯著的監管壁壘保護其業務。因此，在專利和監管這兩個維度上，Gartner 的護城河較為薄弱。","comment_en":"Gartner's core competency lies in its research methodologies, databases, and analyst expertise, rather than patented or licensed technologies. While its research methodologies may possess some uniqueness, they do not constitute a patent moat in the strict sense and are susceptible to imitation or the development of similar analytical frameworks by competitors. Industry regulation also has a relatively minor impact, with no significant regulatory barriers protecting its business. Therefore, Gartner's moat is relatively weak in terms of patents and regulation."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"客戶在轉換到其他研究機構時面臨較高的轉換成本。這不僅體現在重新學習和適應新機構的研究方法和數據標準上，更重要的是，Gartner 的研究報告和數據已深度融入客戶的決策流程和知識體系中。一旦採用 Gartner 的分析，企業將投入大量時間和資源來理解和應用這些信息。更換供應商意味著需要重新建立信任、驗證數據，並可能影響現有的項目進度和決策的連續性，這些都構成了顯著的轉換障礙。","comment_en":"Clients face high switching costs when moving to other research firms. This is not only reflected in the need to relearn and adapt to new firms' research methodologies and data standards but, more importantly, Gartner's research reports and data are deeply integrated into clients' decision-making processes and knowledge systems. Once Gartner's analysis is adopted, companies invest significant time and resources to understand and apply this information. Changing vendors means rebuilding trust, validating data, and potentially impacting existing project timelines and decision continuity, all of which constitute significant switching barriers."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":4,"comment_zh":"Gartner 的網絡效應相對有限。雖然其研究報告的廣泛引用和行業內的聲譽可以間接形成一種信息傳播的網絡，但這並非典型的網絡效應，即用戶越多，產品或服務價值越高的情況。客戶之間並不存在直接的互動來增強服務價值。然而，其研究的普及度和行業標準的確立，確實能鞏固其市場地位，但這種效應的強度不如社交媒體或市場平台類型的網絡效應。","comment_en":"Gartner's network effects are relatively limited. While the widespread citation of its research reports and its industry reputation can indirectly form an information dissemination network, this is not a typical network effect where more users directly increase the value of the product or service. There is no direct interaction among clients that enhances service value. However, the prevalence of its research and the establishment of industry standards do solidify its market position, but the strength of this effect is not comparable to network effects found in social media or marketplace platforms."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Gartner 在規模經濟方面具有一定的優勢。作為全球領先的 IT 研究機構，其龐大的客戶基礎和數據收集能力使其能夠攤薄固定成本，如研發、數據採集和分析師團隊的薪酬。這種規模使得 Gartner 能夠以相對較低的單位成本提供服務，並持續投入資源以保持其研究的領先地位。相較於小型競爭對手，Gartner 在獲取數據、吸引頂尖人才方面也更具優勢，從而形成成本上的競爭力。","comment_en":"Gartner possesses certain advantages in economies of scale. As a leading global IT research firm, its vast client base and data collection capabilities allow it to spread fixed costs, such as R&D, data acquisition, and analyst compensation. This scale enables Gartner to provide services at a relatively lower unit cost and continuously invest resources to maintain its research leadership. Compared to smaller competitors, Gartner also has an advantage in acquiring data and attracting top talent, thus forming a cost competitiveness."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Gartner 的業務模式並非依賴於特定的地理位置或獨特的實體資產。其價值主要體現在無形資產，如知識產權、品牌聲譽和分析師團隊。雖然 Gartner 在全球範圍內開展業務，並擁有廣泛的客戶群，但其服務本質上是可跨地域提供的，並不存在因地理位置而形成的獨特壁壘。競爭對手可以通過建立全球性的研究網絡來複製其地理覆蓋範圍。","comment_en":"Gartner's business model does not rely on specific geographic locations or unique physical assets. Its value is primarily embodied in intangible assets such as intellectual property, brand reputation, and its analyst team. Although Gartner operates globally and has an extensive client base, its services are inherently cross-geographically deliverable, and there are no unique barriers formed by geographic location. Competitors can replicate its geographic coverage by establishing global research networks."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Gartner 在營運效率方面表現出色。公司透過標準化的研究流程、先進的數據分析工具以及高效的全球化運營體系，能夠持續產出高質量的研究報告和服務。其對數據的有效收集、整合與分析能力，以及將這些洞察轉化為客戶價值的效率，是其核心競爭力之一。持續的技術投入和流程優化，確保了其在快速變化的 IT 環境中保持領先，並有效控制成本，實現了卓越的營運效率。","comment_en":"Gartner demonstrates excellent operational efficiency. Through standardized research processes, advanced data analytics tools, and an efficient global operating system, the company consistently produces high-quality research reports and services. Its ability to effectively collect, integrate, and analyze data, and efficiently translate these insights into client value, is one of its core competencies. Continuous investment in technology and process optimization ensures its leadership in the rapidly changing IT landscape and effective cost control, achieving outstanding operational efficiency."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Gartner 在資本配置方面展現了穩健的策略。公司歷史上透過戰略性併購來擴張其服務範圍和市場份額，同時也注重有機增長。其自由現金流充裕，並能有效用於回購股票、支付股息以及再投資於核心業務，以維持其研究的領先地位。管理層在平衡股東回報與長期業務發展之間取得了良好的平衡，顯示出對資本配置的審慎態度和執行力。","comment_en":"Gartner exhibits a sound strategy in capital allocation. Historically, the company has expanded its service scope and market share through strategic acquisitions, while also focusing on organic growth. It generates ample free cash flow, which is effectively used for share repurchases, dividend payments, and reinvestment in its core business to maintain its research leadership. Management has achieved a good balance between shareholder returns and long-term business development, demonstrating a prudent attitude and execution capability in capital allocation."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Gartner 擁有極高的客戶留存率，這得益於其研究的深度、廣度和持續的價值輸出。一旦客戶習慣了 Gartner 的分析框架和數據，並將其融入日常運營，他們便很難輕易轉向其他供應商。續訂率高是其業務模式穩健性的重要指標。公司透過持續的客戶溝通、服務升級和針對性解決方案，不斷鞏固客戶關係，確保了客戶的長期忠誠度。","comment_en":"Gartner enjoys very high customer retention rates, attributable to the depth, breadth, and continuous value delivery of its research. Once clients become accustomed to Gartner's analytical frameworks and data and integrate them into their daily operations, it becomes difficult for them to easily switch to other vendors. High renewal rates are a key indicator of its business model's stability. The company continuously strengthens customer relationships through ongoing client communication, service upgrades, and tailored solutions, ensuring long-term customer loyalty."},"m10_durability":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Gartner 的業務模式具有相當的持久性。儘管科技行業變化迅速，但對獨立、權威的 IT 研究和諮詢的需求始終存在。Gartner 作為行業領導者，其品牌聲譽和客戶關係構成了穩固的壁壘，使其能夠抵禦市場波動和新興競爭者的挑戰。只要其能持續保持研究的前瞻性和質量，並適應技術趨勢，其核心業務的持久性將得到保障。","comment_en":"Gartner's business model possesses considerable durability. Despite the rapid changes in the technology industry, the demand for independent, authoritative IT research and consulting remains constant. As an industry leader, Gartner's brand reputation and client relationships form a solid barrier, enabling it to withstand market fluctuations and challenges from emerging competitors. As long as it can continuously maintain the foresight and quality of its research and adapt to technological trends, the durability of its core business will be assured."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Gartner 的護城河主要建立在其強大的品牌聲譽、深厚的專業知識以及由此產生的客戶轉換成本之上，形成了一種類似於「收費橋」的商業模式。客戶高度依賴其獨立分析來做出關鍵決策，難以替代。雖然其規模帶來了一定的成本優勢和營運效率，但缺乏專利或網絡效應等更為嚴格的壁壘。整體而言，Gartner 擁有一個堅固但非無懈可擊的經濟護城河，其持久性取決於持續的創新和對行業趨勢的適應能力。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Gartner's moat is primarily built upon its strong brand reputation, deep expertise, and the resulting customer switching costs, forming a business model akin to a 'toll bridge.' Clients heavily rely on its independent analysis for critical decision-making, making it difficult to substitute. While its scale provides certain cost advantages and operational efficiencies, it lacks more stringent barriers like patents or network effects. Overall, Gartner possesses a solid, though not impenetrable, economic moat, the durability of which depends on continuous innovation and its ability to adapt to industry trends.","evidenceHash":"ae625c1b732c5784510e9f7d5a5d987bc95f33c42501dd69c2e63222a6711332","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":7,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"safe","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-27T15:49:45.333Z","evidenceHash":"bca32cba98c4262f10ec734c294e095c79331ddb3b7a03782ee4139989b26615"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-27T15:49:45.333Z","evidenceHash":"bca32cba98c4262f10ec734c294e095c79331ddb3b7a03782ee4139989b26615"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/IT.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/IT.png","website":"https://www.gartner.com","ceo":"Eugene A. Hall","full_time_employees":"19285","description":"Gartner, Inc. functions as a premier research and advisory enterprise, extending its reach across the United States, Canada, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and various international markets. Its operations are structured into three main divisions: Research, Conferences, and Consulting. The Research division primarily offers a subscription service, enabling on-demand access to extensive published studies, data, industry benchmarks, and direct consultations with its expert network. The Conferences segment provides a platform for business professionals to acquire new knowledge, share insights, and foster connections. Lastly, the Consulting segment furnishes clients with market research, bespoke analyses, and direct, on-site support services. This segment specifically addresses critical IT challenges, offering practical strategies for areas such as optimizing IT expenditures, managing digital transformation, and enhancing IT sourcing processes. Founded in 1979, Gartner, Inc. has its corporate base in Stamford, Connecticut.","description_en":"Gartner, Inc. functions as a premier research and advisory enterprise, extending its reach across the United States, Canada, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and various international markets. Its operations are structured into three main divisions: Research, Conferences, and Consulting. The Research division primarily offers a subscription service, enabling on-demand access to extensive published studies, data, industry benchmarks, and direct consultations with its expert network. The Conferences segment provides a platform for business professionals to acquire new knowledge, share insights, and foster connections. Lastly, the Consulting segment furnishes clients with market research, bespoke analyses, and direct, on-site support services. This segment specifically addresses critical IT challenges, offering practical strategies for areas such as optimizing IT expenditures, managing digital transformation, and enhancing IT sourcing processes. Founded in 1979, Gartner, Inc. has its corporate base in Stamford, Connecticut.","description_zh":"Gartner, Inc.（美股代碼：IT）為 Technology 領域之重要企業，專注於 Information Technology Services 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"56 Top Gallant Road","city":"Stamford","state":"CT","zip":"06902-7700","country":"US","phone":"203 316 1111","full_address":"56 Top Gallant Road, Stamford, CT 06902-7700, US","range_52w":"124.25-256.9","year_high":256.9,"year_low":124.25,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":124.25,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"Rupani Altaf","title":"officer: EVP, Chief Information Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":165,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"Rupani Altaf","title":"officer: EVP, Chief Information Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"F-InKind","shares":60,"price":207.31,"total_val":0.01},{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"Rupani Altaf","title":"officer: EVP, Chief Information Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":165,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"FERGUSON DIANA SUE","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"J-Other","shares":139,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"FERGUSON DIANA SUE","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":139,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"FERGUSON DIANA SUE","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"J-Other","shares":139,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"PAGLIUCA STEPHE